<title>USA: Molecular Bio disappointed by court ruling.</title>
<headline>Molecular Bio disappointed by court ruling.</headline>
<dateline>SAN DIEGO 1997-04-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Molecular Biosystems Inc Tuesday said it is disappointed a court enjoined the Food and Drug Administration from continuing its review of approving the company's second-generation contrast agent, FS069.</p>
<p>In a statement, the company said District Court Judge Paul Friedman ordered the FDA to preserve the status quo pending FDA action on Citizens' Petitions.</p>
<p>In February, the Radiology Device Advisory Panel of the FDA voted to recommend approval of FS069 without conditions. The company believes the FDA was correct in regulating FS069 and its predecessor product, ALBUNEX, as medical devices.</p>
</text>
